A||||9||SteveJ||Web site design -  soap box ||||8||
Z||000000||SteveJ||02-22-2001||07:56 AM||||When designing your own web site keep in mind that navigation thru the site should be easy and intuitive. You should have return links on every page if you can or at least a return to home link. Links in dark colors on a dark background are a problem as are red text. Got any idea how many colorblind people there are? And then there is the issue of all that busy wallpaper in the background. Beautiful Fiero logos no doubt but when it confuses the message, well you know what you are trying to say but the reader is lost trying to decipher your message.<P>I spend a lot of time on the computer here in the frozen north and when I see long passages in red . . . well it isn't printable.<P>ok, soap box time over.||||reg||8
Z||000001||Tigger||02-22-2001||08:54 AM||||One of my "web" peeves is text that is the same color as the background.  I can't tell you how many times I've had to highlight text and say, "Oh, there it is."||||reg||1
Z||000002||TwisT||02-22-2001||09:57 AM||||Web design is something I happen to be really good at.  Unfortunatly,  not everyone is necessarily thinking of "readability" and "efficient navigation" when designing their web pages.  Rather,  they concentrate on the "flash" effect,  or in other words,  fancy animations and large pictures that take too long to download.  I love surfing Fiero sites but am always running into those sites that are down right frustrating to look at.<P>Unfortunately,  it's something we'll have to live with.  <P>Brett||||reg||1
Z||000003||Songman||02-22-2001||11:54 AM||||It is true... all of the neat tricks in the world can make a web site look good but if it takes too long to load no one will ever see it.<P>I have all of those fancy programs like Flash but never use them. The majority of web surfers are still on fairly slow connections. And with all that is available on the web, they are not willing to wait for all of that fluff..<P>Make it pretty, but also make it useful...<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/songman_1.gif"> <BR><A HREF="http://members.home.com/tnfieros" TARGET=_blank>Tennessee Fiero Owners</A>||||reg||1
Z||000004||tgowens||02-22-2001||12:06 PM||||Good points to ponder.......as a web designer  (West Highland Graphics & Design)  <A HREF="http://www.whgraphics.com" TARGET=_blank>www.whgraphics.com</A>  I have designed several sites including my own  <A HREF="http://www.tgowens.com/fiero" TARGET=_blank>www.tgowens.com/fiero</A>  as well as Fiero club sites.......we sometimes forget about the file size on graphics (I know my sites are laden with photos) but the thing I try for the most is to make them easy to navigate and also design them for cross-browser functionality so that they are viewable in any browser......||||reg||1
Z||000005||DaRkLoRD||02-22-2001||03:55 PM||||I've started messing around in Flash a bit, but I still prefer plain old imagemaps for my menus, etc.. Another thing I always do, is NEVER use a background image directly under text.. If I am going to use a background, I put the text in a table, with a solid colored background.. I often have to select text to read it.<BR>another thing I can't stand is bright blue text on a brighr red page.. Maybe I'm just weird, but I find that extremely hard on the eyes..<P>Also.. having a pirated copy of Photoshop, or even a demo of PSP, and an html editor does NOT make someone a web designer.. I've been doing this stuff for almost 6 years now (started summer of 95) and I'm still not an expert, but I can get by.. it makes me sick when I see people offering their services, and they haven't got any samples of their work, and no past references, no experience, etc. There are some talented web designers on this forum (jackal, tgowens, songman and a few others) and a lot of people who aren't pros, yet know enough to keep the site simple.. then there are others who have a million animated icons, blinking "under construction" images.. fancy javascript applets that crash half the systems that try to view it.. mismatched graphics.. etc.<P>And a LOT of sites have the email listed as "webmaster@whatever.com"... I used to have that, but I got over it when I was 16... now the email on my business site just says "info@digitalfusion.on.ca" and my Fiero site actually has my real address, with my name on it.. I even talked to one guy who thought he was so cool cause he had a website, he changed his ICQ name to "webmaster"... LOL.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>ok, that's hopefully my last rant for the day.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>------------------<BR>  <A HREF="mailto:steve@fieroproject.com">steve@fieroproject.com</A>  <BR><A HREF="http://www.fieroproject.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fieroproject.com</A>||||reg||13
Z||000006||SteveJ||02-22-2001||04:06 PM||||tgowens I love your web site. Great pictures and story. I have a cable modem and it took a while to load all the graphics so maybe break ‘em up into pages. I put it on my favorites list because of all the great pictures. ||||reg||1
Z||000007||tgowens||02-22-2001||06:03 PM||||SteveJ, thanks! Breaking the Fiero site into pages is the next project since it is a continuing saga but I have had to "back burner" it recently since some of my commercial projects are leading the way right now.........for example, the Paderewski Festival  <A HREF="http://www.paderewskifestival.org" TARGET=_blank>www.paderewskifestival.org</A>  will be held in the latter part of March so there is a lot of updating, etc going on with that one. I am also under contract with Integrated Waste Management Authority of San Luis Obispo County (IWMA)  <A HREF="http://www.iwma.com/" TARGET=_blank>www.iwma.com/</A>  and the complexity of the site requires quite a bit of maintenance (check out the mouseovers on the index tabs! -- no javascript, just html for the effect......) -- anyway, thanks for the suggestion and believe me, I will get to it someday........the woes of a commercial web designer are just that their own sites sometimes take a back seat to the commercial work!||||reg||1
Z||000008||Gasolene||02-23-2001||12:56 AM||||I'm a newbie at web page design.  Let me know what you think. <A HREF="http://www.angelfire.com/ab4/fierostereo/index.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.angelfire.com/ab4/fierostereo/index.html</A> ||||reg||1
Z||000009||Robert||02-23-2001||11:23 PM||||I'm still spending more time playing with my tennis club's website <A HREF="http://www.wcrc.net," TARGET=_blank>www.wcrc.net,</A>  than playing tennis this winter. The weather out here in California is nothing but rain, rain, rain.  At least I finally figured out that if I park my 87GT with the front pointed downhill, the sunroof doesn’t leak in the rain.  You won’t believe how much rainwater Mr. Mike’s seats will hold.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>Later<P>Robert<BR><P>------------------<BR>          <IMG SRC="http://canterburytrails.com/photo/T2.GIF"> <P> “If you don’t look for that parking space near the entrance, you’ll never get it”||||reg||2
